":"Proposed massing artillery behind Armistead and Wright to fire across the Federal position"}]]}],["$","div","Division in Jackson’s column-Maj. Gen. D. H. Hill",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Division in Jackson’s column"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Maj. Gen. D. H. Hill"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"Warned Lee about the ground; his seven batteries lacked ammunition after White Oak Swamp"}]]}],["$","div","Army artillery reserve-Brig. Gen. William N. Pendleton",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Army artillery reserve"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Brig. Gen. William N. Pendleton"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"Six batteries remained unused after Pendleton failed to establish contact with Lee"}]]}],["$","div","Assistant adjutant general on Lee’s staff-Col. Robert H. Chilton",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Assistant adjutant general on Lee’s staff"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Col. Robert H. Chilton"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"Drafted the order linking a successful bombardment, Armistead’s advance, and a general attack"}]]}]]]}]
